SmartSessionEmissary::isValidSignatureWithSender
├── given the ERC-7739 detection hash
│   └── it returns 0x77390002
├── given ERC-7739 mode (0x01)
│   ├── when signature is valid
│   │   └── it returns ERC1271_MAGIC_VALUE
│   ├── when session validator rejects signature
│   │   └── it returns INVALID_SIGNATURE
│   ├── when sender is the SmartSessionEmissary itself
│   │   └── it returns INVALID_SIGNATURE
│   ├── when permissionId is invalid
│   │   └── it returns INVALID_SIGNATURE
│   ├── when signature is malformed
│   │   └── it returns INVALID_SIGNATURE
│   ├── when content type does not match enabled content
│   │   └── it returns INVALID_SIGNATURE
│   ├── when content type is not enabled for session
│   │   └── it returns INVALID_SIGNATURE
│   ├── when signature is wrapped with ERC6492
│   │   └── it returns ERC1271_MAGIC_VALUE
│   ├── when hash is not the app hash of the signed contents
│   │   └── it returns INVALID_SIGNATURE
│   ├── when contents description is empty
│   │   └── it returns INVALID_SIGNATURE
│   ├── when header is exactly 64 bytes
│   │   └── it returns ERC1271_MAGIC_VALUE
│   ├── when header is 63 bytes
│   │   └── it returns INVALID_SIGNATURE
│   ├── when the struct has several fields
│   │   └── it returns ERC1271_MAGIC_VALUE
│   ├── when the encodeData word count is wrong
│   │   └── it returns INVALID_SIGNATURE
│   ├── when the struct has no fields
│   │   └── it returns ERC1271_MAGIC_VALUE
│   ├── when appended data exceeds the signature
│   │   └── it returns INVALID_SIGNATURE
│   ├── when header is shorter than 64 bytes
│   │   └── it returns INVALID_SIGNATURE
│   ├── when app domain separator is zero
│   │   └── it returns INVALID_SIGNATURE
│   └── when contents type does not match the signed struct
│       └── it returns INVALID_SIGNATURE
├── given direct mode (0x00)
│   ├── when domain zero is enabled
│   │   ├── when signature is valid
│   │   │   └── it returns ERC1271_MAGIC_VALUE
│   │   └── when session validator rejects signature
│   │       └── it returns INVALID_SIGNATURE
│   └── when domain zero is not enabled
│       └── it returns INVALID_SIGNATURE
└── given unknown mode (0xFF)
    └── it returns INVALID_SIGNATURE